#IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES
		@ENLARGED_WEAPONS
				1. Draw the texture of the weapon. Make sure they are in size of 8x8, 16x16, 32x32, 64x64, 128x128, etc. The size = 2^n [n ∈ ℝ | n >= 0];
				2. Import the texture to Blockbench and extrude it.
				3. Go to Display tag.
				3-1. [Tools] -> [Optimize]. If you don't see this option, go to [Files] -> [Plugins...] and search and download [Optimize] plugin.
				NOTE: Missing channels indicates the value is 0.
				SCALE_FACTOR = width_of_new_texture / 16;
				4. For right hand third-person display: Tx, Ty, and Tz: Depends on weapon's size. Ry: 90, Rz: 45, Sx = Sy = Sz = SCALE_FACTOR;
				5. For left hand third-person display: Tx, Ty, and Tz: Same as the one above it. Ry: 90, Rz: -45, Sx = Sy = Sz = SCALE_FACTOR;
				6. For right hand first-person display: Tx, Ty, and Tz: Adjust them until they hit the window. Ry: 90, Rz: 45, Sx = Sy = Sz = SCALE_FACTOR / (4 / 3);
				7. For left hand first-person display: Tx, Ty, and Tz: Adjust them until they hit the window. Ry: 90, Rz: -45, Sx = Sy = Sz = SCALE_FACTOR / (4 / 3);
				8. Skip the Head.
				9. For the ground, adjust the size of the weapon based on your preference.
				10. Skip the Frame, Shelf, and GUI.
				11. File -> Export -> Export Block/Item Model -> Select desired location. (In this case export it to the item model json folder).
				12. Open the exported json file.
				13. Go to the "textures" -> "0" and "particle"
				14. Make sure "0" and "particle" have the same format: <YOUR_MOD_ID>:item/<NAME_OF_YOUR_WEAPON_TEXTURE>, if not, fix them.
				15. Save the file if you do any changes.
				16. You're done! :D
				
		@MODDED_ENTITY_MODELS_&_ANIMATIONS
				1. Go to [File] -> [Plugins...] and make sure you have [Fabric Modded Entity] downloaded.
				2. Go to [File] -> [Project...] and check the [Export Version]. Make sure the [Export Version] is [Forge 1.17+ (Mojmaps)]. We set this despite we are using Fabric API to develop Minecraft mods. For some reason, [Fabric 1.17+] is still using the old model classes, which will give you tons of error messages when you paste the model class inside modern Fabric dev environment. Make sure you first save this model file in a place OTHER THAN your mod project folder.
				3. Go to [Animate] tab and find [Export Modded Entity Animations]. Make sure everything is selected. Click [Confirm] and save this file in a place OTHER THAN in your mod project folder.
				4. Copy and paste the model and animation class. Stay organized!
				5. Fix any error messages that pops out in your code editing workspace.
				6. You're done! :D
				
		@BLOCK_MODELS
				1. Open Blockbench and select [Java Block/Item]. 
				2. Choose the format Version as [1.21.11 - 26.2].
				3. Choose the UV option as [Box UV]
				4. Make sure your model faces in the [+Z] direction. This is important!
